# HP48gII full stock-launch probe: ARMToolbox48 -> hpclang HPC1.
2000 tap f6
4000 tap f6
# Factory default is ALG; use RPN for the stack-based library install.
5000 tap mode
5500 tap neg
6000 tap f6
7000 capture home-rpn
# Configure wire I/O to Serial.
8000 tap files
9500 tap down
10000 tap enter
11500 tap down
12000 tap down
12500 tap down
13000 tap down
14000 tap enter
16000 tap up
17000 tap f2
18000 tap down
18500 tap enter
20000 tap enter
# Start stock Kermit server.
22000 tap files
23500 tap down
24000 tap enter
25000 tap down
25500 tap down
26000 tap down
26500 tap down
27000 tap down
28000 tap enter
30000 capture server-serial
# Host sends L275 and HPCLANG, then FINISHes. Allow worst-case retry time.
95000 capture after-transfer
# Install ARMToolbox48 Library 275 into Port 0. With both variables present,
# HPCLANG is F1 and L275 is F2 in the HOME VAR menu.
96000 tap var
97000 capture vars-before-install
98000 tap f2
99000 capture l275-stack
100000 tap zero
101000 tap enter
102000 capture port-zero-stack
103000 tap sto
105000 capture stored
107000 chord on f3
113000 capture after-warmstart
# L275 moved to Port 0; HPCLANG remains the first HOME variable.
114000 tap var
115000 capture vars-after-install
116000 tap f1
118000 capture hpclang-stack
# Library 275 is the first LIB entry; ARMTo exposes PrRUN on F1.
120000 chord rshift two
121500 capture lib-menu
122500 tap f1
124000 capture armtoolbox
125000 tap f1
128000 monitor 60000
